[110.510743, "o", "s the next pointers until it reaches the end.\\n\\nBut during iteration, the linked list may be modified, so the pointer must be updated accordingly.\\n\\nAlternatively, during processing a node u in the queue, we can iterate through all nodes in the linked list and check if they are adjacent to u.\\n\\nHere\\'s how the code could look:\\n\\nimport sys\\nfrom sys import stdin\\n\\ndef main():\\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(1 << 25)\\n    n, m = map(int, stdin.readline().split())\\n    non_edges = [set() for _ in range(n)]\\n    for _ in range(m):\\n        x, y = map(int, stdin.readline().split())\\n        x -= 1\\n        y -= 1\\n        non_edges[x].add(y)\\n        non_edges[y].add(x)\\n    \\n    # Initialize linked list\\n    next_node = list(range(1, n+1))\\n    prev_node = list(range(-1, n-1))\\n    visited = [False]*n\\n    components = []\\n    \\n    current = 0\\n    while current < n:\\n        if visited[current]:\\n            current = next_node[current]\\n            continue\\n        # Start BFS\\n        queue = [current]\\n  "]
