[110.511452, "o", "ructure**: Use a linked list to keep track of unvisited nodes. This allows efficient removal of nodes as they are visited.\\n3. **Breadth-First Search (BFS)**: For each unvisited node, perform a BFS to explore all reachable nodes. During BFS, nodes are checked against the non-edges to determine adjacency.\\n4. **Component Tracking**: Track the size of each connected component and sort the results before output.\\n\\n### Solution Code\\n```python\\nimport sys\\nfrom sys import stdin\\n\\ndef main():\\n    input = sys.stdin.read().split()\\n    ptr = 0\\n    n = int(input[ptr])\\n    ptr += 1\\n    m = int(input[ptr])\\n    ptr += 1\\n\\n    non_edges = [set() for _ in range(n)]\\n    for _ in range(m):\\n        x = int(input[ptr])-1\\n        ptr += 1\\n        y = int(input[ptr])-1\\n        ptr += 1\\n        non_edges[x].add(y)\\n        non_edges[y].add(x)\\n\\n    next = list(range(1, n+1))  # Next node in the linked list\\n    prev = list(range(-1, n))   # Previous node in the linked list\\n    visited = [False] * n\\n    component"]
